    <section id="search" aria-labelledby="search-heading">
      <h2 id="search-heading">Finding an internship</h2>
      <p class="callout callout-tip">
        <strong>Do not wait.</strong> Start applying the week you land. And do not hold out
        for a famous name — smaller and mid-sized companies are often the better internship:
        the atmosphere is more personal, colleagues have more time for you, and you get a
        wider range of real tasks.
      </p>

      <h3>Where to look</h3>
      <div class="card-grid three">
        <article class="card compact">
          <h4>Your host university</h4>
          <p>Announcements on the university web page, the notice board, the Career Center, the International Office, and your own professors.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="card compact">
          <h4>The Project Office</h4>
          <p>The GJU Project Office in Magdeburg will send you a list of German companies matching your field of study. Ask for it.</p>
        </article>
