      <h3>Keep a list</h3>
      <p>
        Research is the part most people skimp on. Make one spreadsheet and fill it in the
        moment you send something and the moment anything comes back. Keep every application
        in a single folder on your computer.
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Company, website, contact e-mail</th>
              <th scope="col">What interests you in the offer</th>
              <th scope="col">Sent</th>
              <th scope="col">Follow up</th>
              <th scope="col">Answer</th>
              <th scope="col">Interview</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="dim">…</td><td class="dim">…</td><td class="dim">date</td><td class="dim">date</td><td class="dim">date / yes / no</td><td class="dim">date</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Wait about <strong>two weeks</strong> for an acknowledgement. If nothing arrives,
        call and ask politely whether your application was received and when you can expect
        an answer. Rejections are normal — German students are competing for the same
        places. Ask why, when you can; the next application gets better for it. And answer
        your phone properly during the application phase: take the caller’s name and
        number, and ask again if you did not understand something.
      </p>
