    <section id="contacts" aria-labelledby="contacts-heading">
      <h2 id="contacts-heading">Who to contact</h2>
      <dl class="facts">
        <dt>Office for Industrial Links (OIL), GJU</dt>
        <dd>
          <a href="mailto:oil@gju.edu.jo">oil@gju.edu.jo</a> ·
          <a href="tel:+96264294881">+962 6 429 4881</a> ·
          <a href="http://www.gju.edu.jo/oil" rel="external nofollow">gju.edu.jo/oil</a><br>
          Internship seminars, approval of the placement, and the office that receives your
          certificate and report.
        </dd>

        <dt>Project Office, Magdeburg</dt>
        <dd>
          <a href="mailto:interns@german-jordanian.org">interns@german-jordanian.org</a><br>
          Company address lists for your field, help while you are searching, and a second
          pair of eyes on your CV and cover letter. Stay in touch with them — they can only
          help if you answer e-mails.
        </dd>

        <dt>Your Exchange Coordinator</dt>
        <dd>
          Your academic contact for the whole year in Germany. Approves the Learning
          Agreement and any change to it, approves the internship placement, and checks the
          certificate and report within two months of your return. Each School publishes an
          address of the form <code>exchange.coordinator.&lt;major&gt;@gju.edu.jo</code>.
        </dd>

        <dt>International Office, GJU</dt>
        <dd>
          Runs the nomination, the distribution to partner universities, the university
          applications, Fintiba and the visa process. It does not control the Embassy, the
          <span lang="de">Ausländerbehörde</span>, your accommodation, your enrolment in
          Germany, or the extra fees some host universities charge.
        </dd>

        <dt>The moment you are accepted</dt>
        <dd>
          Tell the Office for Industrial Links and the Project Office in Magdeburg
          immediately, send the company details and contract to your Exchange Coordinator
          for approval, and cancel your other interviews — by phone if you can.
        </dd>
      </dl>
